   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, I&#39;m writing a function to create a block-diagonal matrix.   May one use block() to write values to a sub-block of a matrix?<div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div><br></div><div>Terrance<br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\">Thank you, Terrance Savitsky</div>\r\n</div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "lbGVBkB9DQAJ",
   "from": "Jonah Gabry",
   "author": "fc5d3270037d7478",
   "date": "2016-05-16T17:29:25Z",
   "subject": "Re: May block() be used to write values?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Terrance, <div><br></div><div>We don&#39;t have R-style replacement functions (not sure if that&#39;s on Bob&#39;s long-term to-do list for the language or not), so you can&#39;t do something like </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">block</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>However, recent versions of Stan do allow for much more flexibility with indexing (including for assignment), so I think you should be able to do things like <br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// i,j,k,l integers</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">row_ids</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col_ids</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">//row_ids, col_ids integer arrays</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>that weren&#39;t previously possible. Hope that helps, </div><div><br></div><div>Jonah</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Ki5VZzR-DQAJ",
